kosha air

  -- the gas mixture of earth's atmosphere.
  -- composition: N2 78%, O2 21%, Ar 0.93%, CO2 0.04%, trace gases.
  -- essential for combustion (O2), respiration (O2), and life.
  --
  -- properties:
  --   gas: no fixed shape or volume. fills any container.
  --   density: 1.225 kg/m³ at sea level, 20°C. decreases with altitude.
  --   thermal insulator: k = 0.025 W/mK (lowest of common materials).
  --   transparent and invisible (no absorption in visible range).
  --   Rayleigh scattering: shorter wavelengths scatter more → blue sky.
  --   sound: propagates at 343 m/s in air at 20°C.
  --   pressure: 101325 Pa (1 atm) at sea level. decreases with altitude.
  --   humidity: water vapour content. 100% = saturated = fog/cloud/rain.

